<title>USA: Lockheed Martin wins $75 mln Japan contract.</title>
<headline>Lockheed Martin wins $75 mln Japan contract.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lockheed Martin Corp said on Friday that it received a $75 million contract from Mitsubishi Heavy Industries, as part of its participation in Japan Air Self Defense Force's F-2 production project.</p>
<p>Lockheed said it would produce all the aircraft aft fuselages, wing leading-edge flaps and eight of the 10 left-hand wing boxes for the F-2. The Japanese government planned to produce a total of 130 F-2 aircraft, it said.</p>
<p>It said this contract was the first in what was expected to be more than $2.5 billion in contracts in the next 15 years.</p>
</text>
